{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Professionalism\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Professionalism points can be earned throughout the semester for demonstrating exceptional professionalism to your client, UCA, or Professor Reilly. Taking initiative to go above and beyond basic course requirements is strongly encouraged and will be rewarded. Professionalism points may also be subtracted for actions that are unprofessional (failure to send client emails on time, absence from class, etc.).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Caps}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 There is a cap of {\b +5 points} and {\b -10 points} toward your final grade.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 How to Gain and Lose Professionalism Points\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Attendance}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 To be considered excused, you must email your UCA {\i before} class. Upon approval, your absence may be excused. Students may have one unexcused absence without penalty. Additional unexcused absences will result in the loss of a professionalism point per absence. Repeated lateness will incur point loss.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Class Work Time}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 Class is primarily a period for work time on your projects. You may not leave class early unless you have completed work on all assignments for the week {\i and} there is no more work you could feasibly do on your project. If you have done so, you may ask your UCA for an early exit.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Emails to Client}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 CC your UCA on {\b all} emails with your client, or you will lose one professionalism point per email. Only CC Professor Reilly if your UCA has instructed you to do so. UCAs reserve the right to deduct points for slapdash language or intent in emails to clients.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Emails to UCAs and Professor}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 Exercise professionalism when emailing UCAs and Professor Reilly. UCAs reserve the right to deduct points for slapdash language or intent in emails to Professor Reilly and/or UCAs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Deadlines and Meetings}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 Failure to attend any scheduled meeting \u8212- including meetings with your client, your UCA, Professor Reilly, or an A&S advisor \u8212- will result in a loss of 3 points per meeting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Client Presentation}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 Some clients ask for a presentation of their own. Students who give a presentation to their client earn an extra professionalism point. See the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "assignments/15-final-presentation.qmd"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Final Presentation
}}}
 assignment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Client Evaluation}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 If a client reaches out with a valid and reasonable complaint about your performance or professionalism, this will result in a loss of up to 10 points, at the discretion of your UCA and Professor Reilly.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 {\b Other}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi0 Other exceptional or unprofessional conduct not listed here can result in a gain or loss of professionalism points accordingly, at Professor Reilly\u8217's and the UCAs\u8217' discretion.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Late Assignment Policy\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All assignments must be turned in on time unless otherwise noted or approved. Each day late will be subject to a per-day penalty unless a prior arrangement for an extension is given. Assignments more than 7 days late will not be accepted unless an exception is granted by the Professor.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Blackboard\u8217's assignment portal indicates whether an assignment is late; UCAs will notify you of points lost when an assignment is submitted late. Late penalties only accrue on business days (Monday through Friday). The late penalty for all assignments is {\b one point per late day}, with a maximum of half of the assignment\u8217's points off.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 {\b Note}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li720 \fi0 Extensions may only be granted by Professor Reilly.\par}
